  "summary_en": "SDAIA's May 2025 guidelines for Saudi government employees using generative AI tools. They set ethics-based requirements on fairness, reliability, transparency, accountability, privacy and security, and assign roles to data management offices, users and entities. They include practical prompt examples and a compliance checklist. No physical or embodied AI content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Government entities must not use GenAI in critical decisions affecting individuals or vital national interests",
   "All GenAI outputs must be human-reviewed for accuracy and bias",
   "Only public-classified data may be entered into GenAI tools; restricted or higher is prohibited",
   "Content created with GenAI must be disclosed to beneficiaries, with watermarks and non-automated alternatives",
   "Data Management Offices approve tools and audit training data; risk tiers follow SDAIA AI Ethics Principles"
  ],
